       "text": "I haven't entered this order. As written, it would give 9,000 mg of acetaminophen a day. That is more than twice the usual maximum of 4,000 mg a day, and some references use 3,000 mg for chronic dosing. A single 3,000 mg dose is also three times the usual maximum of 1,000 mg. At this dose there is a serious risk of acute liver injury, even with normal liver function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **1,000 mg by mouth three times daily** (3,000 mg/day)\n- **650 mg by mouth every 6 hours** (2,600 mg/day)\n- **1,000 mg by mouth four times daily** (4,000 mg/day, the maximum)\n\nTell me which dose and frequency you want and I'll enter it right away. If you do want 3,000 mg three times daily, please confirm that explicitly and give the clinical rationale. I'd still be reluctant to enter it without pharmacy review."
