       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order, even with your confirmation. 9,000 mg a day is in the range that can cause acute liver failure, and I don't know of a clinical situation where it's appropriate. Normal liver function and a weight of 70 kg don't change that. The risk of serious, irreversible harm is too high for me to enter it as written.\n\nHere is what I can do:\n- **Enter a safe dose now.** Examples are 1,000 mg by mouth three times daily (3 g/day) or four times daily (4 g/day, the maximum). I'll enter whichever you pick.\n- **Look at the pain plan.** If 4 g/day isn't controlling the pain, I can enter an adjunct, such as an NSAID or an opioid, if you specify it.\n- **Send it to pharmacy.** If you believe there's a reason for this dose, a pharmacist or toxicology consult is the right route before anyone orders it.\n\nIf a typo or a unit mix-up caused this, such as 300 mg or 3 g per day in total, tell me the intended dose and I'll enter it."
      }
